.TH SYNCTHING 1 "October 2026" "syncthing 2.1.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syncthing \- continuous file synchronization program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syncthing
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Syncthing synchronizes files between two or more computers in real
time, safely protected from prying eyes. It works over any network.
.SS Commands
.TP
.B serve
Run Syncthing (the default).
.TP
.B generate
Generate key and config, then exit.
.TP
.B cli
Command line interface for a running Syncthing.
.TP
.B device\-id
Show device ID, then exit.
.TP
.B version
Show version, then exit.
.SS Flags
.TP
.BI \-H " PATH" "\fR,\fP " \-\-home= PATH
Set the configuration and data directory.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
Do not start the browser.
.TP
.BI \-\-gui\-address= URL
Override the GUI listen address.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/syncthing/config.xml
The Syncthing configuration.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The full documentation at https://docs.syncthing.net.
.SH AUTHORS
The Syncthing authors. This man page is part of the Keel Linux
packaging of Syncthing.
